ance it  can bring my men  safely men and women safely into an  environment of an active shooter  and they take those victims out from  that same environment  you just had something where you needed  this vehicle at the stopping shop that  made national news you're able to bring  a suspect  in alive  that vehicle was on the scene in front  if the individuals started to shoot from  the window  and hit somebody this vehicle is going  to get them out safely  it's not used often but when it's needed  it's there for us  as we see this cell phone video and we  see this uh the body camera video  what is it like guys on the street like  that as we see scenarios where you're  wrestling around  and non-compliant suspects it's a  challenging time policing right now  you want to do your job out there and  get the bad guy off the street but the  same time as you said  everyone's videotaping it and monday  morning quarterbacking is something that  is almost deterring us from  deploying the different moves and  techniques that we've been taught  if qualified to community disappear  tomorrow you now have to wonder will you  have a home to go to  at the end of the week or are we going  to be losing our homes and losing  everything that we have and everything  we build up  it's a challenging time it really is  because we all took the job to do the  right thing and that's to help the  community  and now once everyone's watching it on  the news it's  making a second guess every decision you  make  [Music]  special thanks to nassau county police  especially their version of swat for  lebanon helping us out give us an  understanding how hard they train to  make sure everything comes out right  and sometimes you do everything right  and it comes out wrong and we see a lot  of that joining us now a man who knows  all this  he's been studying this uh hot and heavy  for over a year republican senator from  south carolina tim scott  senator want to give people a  perspective from the police o